  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#26296\", \"PowerToys#29364\", \"PowerToys#37938\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been made before. Mouse Without Borders for Android, iPad and other devices is tracked in PowerToys#26296, and similar requests were closed as duplicates of it (e.g. #29364). It is not currently available, so there is nothing to configure. Add your use case or a thumbs-up to #26296 to help prioritize it. Until then, scrcpy can mirror and control an Android phone from your PC, as suggested in that thread. It works by screen mirroring rather than moving the cursor between devices, so it is not the same experience. For seamless cursor switching, Barrier (free) or Synergy (paid) are alternatives mentioned there, though the Barrier and Synergy comments are about Linux and macOS, not phones.\"}",
